From 5c9cdd78a13774dc0f0405e39c4d4b26199d28e1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Richard Rodger <richard@ricebridge.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 18:55:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ci(zig): install Zig into a venv on macOS, where Homebrew's
 pip refuses

test-zig (macos-14) has failed on every commit since #119 merged, and main
has been red with it. The Setup Zig step installs `ziglang` with the runner's
python3, and on macos-14 that python3 is Homebrew's - which marks it
externally managed. pip does not warn there, it exits 1:

    error: externally-managed-environment
    x This environment is externally managed
    `-> To install Python packages system-wide, try brew install ...

The step dies before zig is ever fetched, so nothing after it runs. PEP 668
names the venv as the answer, and a venv needs no extra action.

Scoped to macOS on purpose. The ubuntu and windows legs install into the
runner's tool-cache Python, which carries no such marker and passes today;
this leaves both byte-identical rather than moving three legs to fix one.

lint-zig needs no change: it is ubuntu-only.

Verified locally as far as it can be from outside a macOS runner - the
mechanism itself, venv then `pip install --require-hashes -r
.github/zig-requirements.txt` then the shim, ends in `zig version` printing
0.16.0. The macOS branch condition is the part no local run can reach.
---
 .github/workflows/build.yml | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/.github/workflows/build.yml b/.github/workflows/build.yml
index a77c97d..a823d12 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/build.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/build.yml
@@ -422,6 +422,17 @@ jobs:
         run: |
           set -euo pipefail
           py=python3; command -v python3 >/dev/null 2>&1 || py=python
+          # macos-14's python3 is Homebrew's, and Homebrew marks it externally
+          # managed: `pip install` there does not warn, it exits 1 (PEP 668,
+          # "externally-managed-environment") before zig is ever fetched. A
+          # venv is the documented answer and needs no extra action. Scoped to
+          # macOS on purpose - the ubuntu and windows legs install into the
+          # runner's tool-cache Python, which carries no such marker, and this
+          # leaves those two byte-identical.
+          if [ "$RUNNER_OS" = macOS ]; then
+            "$py" -m venv "$RUNNER_TEMP/zigvenv"
+            py="$RUNNER_TEMP/zigvenv/bin/python"
+          fi
           "$py" -m pip install --disable-pip-version-check --quiet \
             --require-hashes -r "$GITHUB_WORKSPACE/.github/zig-requirements.txt"
           bin="$RUNNER_TEMP/zigbin"; mkdir -p "$bin"
-- 
2.43.0

